C03: a known unsupported contract is neither withdrawn by the catalog verifier nor pre-empted by near names (LIMITS1679)

LIMITS1677 measured the six known-limit contracts: they held when nothing removed them, but the catalog verifier (_catalog_answers_the_request) withdrew the closed limit for a nearby operation that does not serve the request (browser.tabs.list, app.close, audio.volume.adjust) and the model then asked or composed an unauthorized confirmation, and the near-application clarifier asked about another application for the first shell request. A known_unsupported_effect_request contract is the root's finding that no operation serves the request: the verifier no longer withdraws it and the near-name clarifier no longer pre-empts it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


